## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates ability to design safe, scalable canary rollouts for multi-tenant LLM gateways, balancing SLA guarantees, data locality, and observability.

## Key Concepts
- Canary rollout stages and metrics
- Per-tenant isolation and hot-swapping
- SLA-driven rollback and drift detection
- Region-aware routing and audits

## Code Example
```javascript
function canaryRoute(tenant, versionMap){
  // pseudo routing logic
  const stage = tenant.stage;
  const v = versionMap[stage] || versionMap.full;
  return {tenant, version: v};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rollbacks under sudden SLA degradation?
- How do you validate drift metrics across regions without leaking data?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cost- and latency-aware routing in multi-tenant LLM ops, including dynamic model selection and prompt segmentation under burst load.

## Key Concepts
- SLA-driven routing and per-tenant budgets
- Dynamic model variant selection (cost vs. latency)
- Prompt chunking strategies and batching
- Telemetry, drift detection, and resilience under burst traffic

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: select a model variant based on tenant budget and latency target
function selectVariant(tenant, state, latencyTarget) {
  const budgetLeft = state[tenant].budget - state[tenant].spent;
  const withinLatency = state[tenant].avgLatency <= latencyTarget;
  if (budgetLeft > 0 && withinLatency) return 'highQuality';
  if (budgetLeft > 0) return 'balanced';
  return 'cheap';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you ensure fairness when tenants with large budgets dominate capacity?
- How would you validate latency targets under sudden burst traffic?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests handling of data sovereignty, per-tenant policies, auditability, and recovery in a real-world LLM-ops gateway.

## Key Concepts

- Data locality and regional routing
- Per-tenant model versioning
- Configurable data retention and automatic purge
- Tamper-evident, cryptographically signed logs
- Deterministic replay for audits

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: sign and log
function logAudit(entry, key) {
  const payload = JSON.stringify(entry);
  const sig = HMACSHA256(key, payload);
  saveLog({payload, sig, ts: Date.now()});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test purge operations without impacting live traffic?
- How would you handle cross-region latency spikes while preserving policy guarantees?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests cost-aware routing and per-tenant quotas, a practical constraint in real llm-ops gateways.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant budgets and token accounting
- Routing policy using model variants (fast/balanced/cheap)
- Fallback mechanisms and caching
- API surface and minimal test plan

## Code Example

```javascript
function route(request, budget, models){
  const t = request.tokens;
  if (budget.remaining < t) return {model: models.cheap, useCache:true};
  // choose model based on remaining budget
  // ...
  return {model: models.balanced, remaining: budget.remaining - t};
}
```

